    <h2>FAQ<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <details><summary>What is the keypad code in Rooms &amp; Exits Chapter 1 Level 6?</summary><p><b>1496</b>. It goes into the four-digit keypad on the blue ticket machine in the north-east corner of the park, and the same number is painted on the blue ride structure behind the control console next to it.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What are the three numbers in the photo booth?</summary><p><b>20</b>, <b>67</b> and <b>81</b>, left to right. They go into the three two-digit fields across the top of the strength tester, not back into the photo booth.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How do you get the key in Amusement Park?</summary><p>Set the strength tester's panel to 20 / 67 / 81, then hit the punching bag until the score reads <b>2000</b>. The silver key is dispensed at that point.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What does the key unlock?</summary><p>The red arcade cabinet beside the strength tester. Its front panel has a keyhole in the middle; the key opens the cabinet and the bumper-car grid inside pays out the <b>Ring</b> you need for the final ring toss board.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How long does Level 6 take?</summary><p>About five minutes. The recorded run this page is built from finishes at <b>5:06</b>; the two long stretches are the eighteen-tile candy panel and the six-by-six bumper-car grid.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Do I have to spin the prize wheel?</summary><p>No. The wheel takes the coin from the ticket machine and it can land on LOSE, but nothing in the level depends on it. It is the one optional machine in Amusement Park.</p></details>

